01:44:19.140 --> 01:44:27.820
世界は夢を紡ぎ続ける

01:45:08.530 --> 01:45:09.490
I’m back.

01:45:11.200 --> 01:45:12.530
Looks like things are fine.

01:45:14.530 --> 01:45:17.040
You’ve worked hard.

01:45:17.830 --> 01:45:19.830
Though it doesn’t smell like salt,

01:45:19.830 --> 01:45:21.250
I still like the current café.

01:45:21.960 --> 01:45:24.330
It’s in the city, so lots of people gather there.

01:45:26.090 --> 01:45:28.460
Is everyone doing well?

01:45:33.640 --> 01:45:35.140
You look sad.

01:45:36.470 --> 01:45:37.640
She …

01:45:38.140 --> 01:45:40.560
Ever since Ashimori broke her,

01:45:41.180 --> 01:45:42.690
I’ve been feeling insecure.

01:45:43.600 --> 01:45:44.810
They—

01:45:44.810 --> 01:45:46.770
Will they find happiness?

01:45:47.610 --> 01:45:49.480
No matter how many times we try …

01:45:51.650 --> 01:45:54.780
This time round—how many times has it been now?

01:45:55.200 --> 01:45:56.280
Three times …

01:45:56.280 --> 01:45:57.240
Or four …

01:45:58.490 --> 01:45:59.540
They—

01:45:59.540 --> 01:46:01.290
Will they be able to laugh?

01:46:02.870 --> 01:46:03.540
I—

01:46:06.380 --> 01:46:09.130
Your children are laughing …

01:46:09.130 --> 01:46:10.710
Alongside humans.

01:46:12.130 --> 01:46:13.930
I feel insecure.

01:46:13.930 --> 01:46:15.550
It’s unbearable.

01:46:15.550 --> 01:46:16.470
It’s all right.

01:46:17.300 --> 01:46:20.310
Someday, definitely, it will extend beyond the café.

01:46:23.560 --> 01:46:27.060
Something happened today to make me think that.

01:46:27.060 --> 01:46:29.730
Won’t you tell me about it?

01:46:29.730 --> 01:46:32.320
The main character is a certain boy.

01:46:32.740 --> 01:46:35.030
So today’s story is …
